---The persistent DB system provides a way for plugins to store runtime data and preserve it across game sessions,
---making it ideal for storing user-facing plugin settings.
---
---Records are isolated per plugin, preventing plugins from accessing or modifying eachother's data. Records are shared
---by all game clients of the same type on the device, and therefore all characters that are played from the device.
---Records are not shared between beta and live game clients. If you wish for plugins to save their data per-character,
---then you should implement character name or tracking ID as part of storage and retrieval.
---@class PersistentDB
PersistentDB = {}

---Retrieves the entry associated with the provided key and the current plugin from the persistent DB, returning its
---value.
---
---Explicit Data Types: You can explicitly request data of a certain type by using the following aliases: These function
---the same as the general `Get` function, however they also check the data type, returning nil if there's a type
---mismatch.
---@param key string The name associated with a persistent DB entry.
---@return boolean|integer|number|string|table|nil # Value associated with the entry matching the provided key, or nil if there is no such entry. The returned type matches the type originally used when storing that entry.
function PersistentDB:Get(key) end

