---Stores the provided value in the persistent DB, associating it with the specified key and the current plugin.
---
---Explicit Data Types: You can explicitly set data of a certain type by using the following aliases: These function the
---same as the general `Get` function, however they also check the data type, returning nil if there's a type mismatch.
---When using these aliases, make sure you also use the typed `Get` aliases instead of the untyped function. Otherwise
---you may end up storing a different type than what you're expecting, as `Set` may be unable to differentiate between
---`Int` and `Float` for example due to how Lua works.
---@param key string The name associated with a persistent DB entry.
---@param value boolean|integer|number|string|table
---@return boolean
function PersistentDB:Set(key, value) end

